we have to end the sanctuary cities crap  fast fast  there are more than 200 cities and  counties across the US with policies  instructing local law enforcement not to  investigate the immigration status of  suspects or prisoners in their custody  these sanctuary cities are a target of  the GOP this primary season with  candidates jumping to characterize them  as lawless city states whose leaders  have blood on their hands as these  mayors these city officials they are  partners in crime they should be held  criminally liable as accomplices I don't  think you can have whole cities or whole  states just not obeying the law San  Francisco has been a sanctuary city  since 1989 there are 300 of them and  meanwhile what has happened nothing on  July 1st Kate Steinle was walking with  her father along pier 14 in San  Francisco when a bullet ricocheted off  the ground struck her in the back and  killed her the gunman was an illegal  immigrant from Mexico and Juan Francisco  Lopez Sanchez Kate Steinle was hardly  the first case but because she was young  she was attractive the guy who killed  her was about as disgusting as you could  come up with it caught along with the  press and it was a story that you know  had to be covered  Don Rosenberg is an activist affiliated  with Californians for population  stabilization an anti-immigration group  and he writes about the danger of  unlicensed drivers of his website  unlicensed to kill he experienced a  personal tragedy when an illegal  immigrant lacking a driver's license hit  his son with his car and then ran over  him several times trying to escape by  that time a man in the in a car in the  intersection had gotten out and stood in  front of his car and he stopped and his  rear tire was on my son's abdomen took  five people to lift the car off of him  but he was already dead at that point  Rosenberg believes that the common  thread connecting the death of Steinle  and that of his own son is the city of  San Francisco itself a sanctuary city  sanctuary city policies are clearly  illegal obstruction of justice if you or  I tried to  protect somebody in the country  illegally particularly somebody who  would you know committed a crime we  would go to jail that doesn't give the  city the right to do it san Francisco's  sheriff Rossmore karim is at the center  of the media storm that followed the  murder of Kate Steinle after all it was  one of his jails that released Lopez  Sanchez  despite transfer requests from  Immigration and Customs Enforcement  but Mirkarimi says he was following the  law through the last 25 years the City  and County of San Francisco has been  very sensitive to the question of  immigration and to the plight of  undocumented people's about a quarter  century ago a number of laws of just  sanctuary city laws have been passed by  our Board of Supervisors in 2013 a  different kind of law was passed by our  Board of Supervisors and signed into  effect by the current mayor called due  process for all that helps stipulate a  limited interface between law  enforcement and immigration customs and  enforcement so do you believe that  sanctuary city policies make law  enforcement job easier and make the  community safer I do and I think in a  state like California in a city like San  Francisco being on the Pacific Rim and  being such a hub for diverse non-english  speaking immigrant and undocumented  populations you could see the contrast  in years before where there had been no  sanctuary city laws or due process for  all laws where it was actually  undermining and subverting Public Safety  because of the lack of collaboration and  cooperation between government law  enforcement and and those communities  mercury mieze argument that sanctuary  city policies increased cooperation with  law enforcement is difficult to measure  but a survey out of the University of  Illinois found that 45% of Latinos  stated that they are less likely to  voluntarily offer information about  crimes and 45% are less likely to report  a crime because they are afraid the  police will ask them or people they know  about their immigration status and in  general first-generation immigrants a  quarter of whom are undocumented are far  less likely to commit violent or  property  than native-born Americans even if it  was true that illegal aliens committed  less crime than citizens every crime  they commit is an additional crime that  shouldn't have happened it might be true  that if you let fewer people in the  country and reduce the population there  would be fewer crimes overall but this  scenario would likely involve some  combination of mass deportations an  invasive employer verification system  the ability of police to ask for your  citizenship papers at every traffic stop  and billions of dollars more spent on  border control and the bottom line is  that San Francisco is not significantly  more dangerous than non sanctuary cities  of a similar size and in fact  experienced far fewer murders than many  of them it's hard to stop lone wolves  like Lopez Sanchez who didn't have a  violent record his felony record was a  litany of drug charges and illegal  border crossings why he fired a gun on  pier 14 that fateful evening remains a  mystery Kate Steinle death is a terrible  perhaps inexplicable tragedy to just  point finger at sanctuary city or to  vilify because of this tragedy may feel  good and venting about their  frustrations and anger but it's only  going to unravel  I think the good work over all that is  being done to build the kind of trust  that needs to be built with these  communities in the first place  politicians and pundits are always  talking about importance of high-tech  foreigners for the US economy but the  fact of the matter is that low-skilled  immigrants make equally vital  contributions and here are five reasons  why
 

